<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<xsl:stylesheet version="1.1"
	xmlns:xsl="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Transform"
	xmlns:fo="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format"
	exclude-result-prefixes="fo"
	xmlns:fn="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-functions"
	xmlns:java="java">
 
  <xsl:template match="/" name="AAA04F042">
     	   <fo:block>
				<xsl:call-template name="CommonHeader" />
			</fo:block>

          <fo:block text-align="center" margin-left="1.3in" margin-right="1.3in" font-size="12px" font-family="Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif;" space-before="5mm" space-after="5mm" font-weight="bold">

            FLORIDA AMENDATORY ENDORSEMENT


          </fo:block>
          <fo:block padding-left="5pt" font-family="Arial, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif;" font-size="10px" text-align="justify">


            <fo:block space-after="4mm">

              <fo:list-block>
                <fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label>
                    <fo:block>
                      <fo:inline>1.</fo:inline>
                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body>

                    <fo:block space-after="3mm" start-indent="7mm">
                      Section III., Extensions, Paragraph D Extended Reporting Period Extensions, Item 3., <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Retired Insured</fo:inline> Extended Reporting Period, is deleted and replaced wit the following:
                    </fo:block>
				 	<fo:block margin-top="2mm"/>
                    <fo:block font-weight="bold" text-indent="1.5cm" font-size="12px" text-align="left" >3.	Retired Insured Extended Reporting Period</fo:block>
				 	<fo:block margin-top="2mm"/>
				 
				 	<fo:block font-size="10px" start-indent="2cm" text-align="left" >Provided this policy (a) has not been cancelled for nonpayment of premium or Deductible and (b) no other Extended Reporting Period is in effect and (c) this policy remains in force as to all other <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insureds</fo:inline>, except in the case where all <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insureds</fo:inline> are <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Retired Insureds</fo:inline>, a <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Retired Insured</fo:inline> shall have the right to purchase an unlimited extension of time to report <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claims</fo:inline> that are first made against such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Retired Insured</fo:inline> and reported to the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> after the effective date of retirement by reason of negligent acts, errors or omissions alleged to have been committed subsequent to the applicable <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Prior Acts Date</fo:inline>, but before the effective date of retirement and not otherwise excluded by the agreements, conditions and exclusions of this policy. The additional premium for this <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Retired Insured</fo:inline> Extended Reporting Period shall be a percentage of the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Retired Insured’s</fo:inline> proportionate share of the annual premium (and a different percentage of the annual premium in the case where all <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insureds</fo:inline> are <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Retired Insureds</fo:inline>) and is due and payable to the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> no later than thirty days after the effective date of retirement, or cessation of the practice of accountancy.</fo:block>
				 
                  </fo:list-item-body>
                </fo:list-item>
                
                <fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label>
                    <fo:block>
                      <fo:inline>2.</fo:inline>
                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body>

                    <fo:block space-after="3mm" start-indent="7mm">
                     Section VI., General Conditions, Paragraph H. Authorization and Sole Agent, is amended by deletion of these words where they appear in the sentence: “… and warranties…” .

                    </fo:block>
                    
                  </fo:list-item-body>
                </fo:list-item>
                
                 <fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label>
                    <fo:block>
                      <fo:inline>3.</fo:inline>
                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body>

                    <fo:block space-after="3mm" start-indent="7mm">
                     Section III., Extensions, B. Spousal and Domestic partner Extension is deleted and replaced with the following new B.:
                    </fo:block>
                    <fo:block margin-top="2mm"/>
                    <fo:block text-indent="1.5cm" font-size="12px" text-align="left" >B. Spouse Extension</fo:block>
				 	<fo:block margin-top="2mm"/>
				 
				 	<fo:block font-size="10px" start-indent="2cm" text-align="left" >If a <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline> is made against the lawful spouse of an <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> which includes a <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline> for a negligent act, error or omission made against an <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline>, then such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline> shall be deemed a <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline> made against such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline>, provided his or her lawful spouse accepts the same legal counsel as the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> and that such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline> is made solely by reason of such lawful spouse’s status as such. This extension, however, shall not apply to any <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline> alleging any negligent act, error or omission committed or alleged to have been committed by the lawful spouse of an <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
				 
                  </fo:list-item-body>
                </fo:list-item>
                
                
                 <fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label>
                    <fo:block>
                      <fo:inline>4.</fo:inline>
                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body>

                    <fo:block space-after="3mm" start-indent="7mm">
                    Section V., Exclusions, is amended by deletion of (a) and (b) in exclusion 9 and replacing with the following (a) and (b):
                    </fo:block>
                    <fo:block margin-top="2mm"/>
                    <fo:block font-size="10px" start-indent="2cm" text-align="left" >(a) such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> or his/her spouse controlled or owned more than 10% equity interest, operated or managed such person or entity; or,</fo:block>
                    <fo:block font-size="10px" start-indent="2cm" text-align="left" >(b) such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> or his/her spouse was a  partner, member, director, officer or employee of such person or entity:</fo:block>
                    
                  </fo:list-item-body>
                </fo:list-item>
                
                <fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
                <fo:list-item-label>
                <fo:block>
                5.
                </fo:block>
                </fo:list-item-label>
                <fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
	                <fo:block space-after="4mm">
	                	Section V., Exclusions, is amended by deletion of (a) in exclusion 10 and replacing with the following (a):
	                </fo:block>
	                <fo:block margin-top="2mm"/>
                    <fo:block font-size="10px" start-indent="2cm" text-align="left" >(a) an executor, administrator or personal representative of an estate or as a trustee if the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> or its spouse was a beneficiary or distributee of that estate or trust; or,</fo:block>
                </fo:list-item-body>
                </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
                	
                
	           	<fo:block margin-top="6mm"/>
				      <fo:block text-align="left" font-size="10px" >All other terms, conditions and limitations of the policy remain unaltered.</fo:block>
				      <fo:block margin-top="6mm"/>
				       <fo:block>
				       <fo:table  text-align="center">
					    <fo:table-column column-width = "80mm" />
				        <fo:table-column column-width = "80mm" />
				       
